{"name":"Blue Flag","hex":"#3b506f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue flag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An award given to European beaches, based on cleanliness and water quality.","A driver notification indicating a faster vehicle is coming up from behind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_flag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Flag award","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Flag is a certification by the Foundation for Environmental Education (FEE) that a beach, marina, or sustainable boating tourism operator meets its standards. The Blue Flag is a trademark owned by FEE, which is a not-for-profit, non-governmental organisation consisting of more than 100 organisations spreading 81 countries. As of 2025, Spain is the country with the most Blue Flag beaches in the world, with 642 Blue Flags and 749 awards in total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Blue_Flag_Logo.svg/330px-Blue_Flag_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Flag_award","wikidata":"Q458651"},{"title":"Blue Flag (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Flag  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Kaito, the creator of Cross Manage. It was serialized digitally on Shōnen Jump+ from February 2017 to April 2020, and publisher Shueisha later collected the chapters in eight tankōbon volumes. A slice-of-life manga set in a high school, Blue Flag tells the story of a group of friends who must navigate personal difficulties, societal expectations, and their feelings for and about each other."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/Blue_Flag_%28manga%29_vol._1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Flag_(manga)","wikidata":"Q48762057"},{"title":"Flag","blocks":[{"text":"A flag is a piece of fabric with distinctive colours and design, often flown from a pole and used for symbolic, signalling, or decorative purposes. The term flag is also used to refer to the graphic design employed on such pieces of fabric. The study of flags is known as \"vexillology\" from the Latin vexillum, meaning \"flag\" or \"banner\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg/330px-United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag","wikidata":"Q14660"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg/500px-File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg/1280px-File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg/500px-File_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._%287223447270%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue Flag in Malia, Crete","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFile_by_Alexander_Baranov_-_._(7223447270).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lenini_m%C3%A4etipp_%28J._K%C3%BCnnap%29.jpg/500px-Lenini_m%C3%A4etipp_%28J._K%C3%BCnnap%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lenini_m%C3%A4etipp_%28J._K%C3%BCnnap%29.jpg/1280px-Lenini_m%C3%A4etipp_%28J._K%C3%BCnnap%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lenini_m%C3%A4etipp_%28J._K%C3%BCnnap%2